      "role": "user",
      "content": "you keep saying it's temporary, but you don't get it. life isn't a movie where everything gets fixed in the end. i've spent my whole life building something, and it took one week for everyone to decide i was a monster. i look in the mirror and i don't even recognize the person looking back because that person doesn't exist to anyone else. it feels more honest to just... stop pretending. like, if the social version of me is already dead, why is the actual me still forced to keep performing this role? it's exhausting.",
